# CSS-FLEXBOX#flex-baselines

**Flex Container Baselines** (heading)

**SHA**: hash:6331964c4098d548ddb5cb8ae86140e48992e04be8e3a237b82068f98d773f54

## Content

In order for a [flex container](CSS-FLEXBOX#flex-container) to itself [participate in baseline alignment](CSS-FLEXBOX#baseline-participation) (e.g. when the flex container is itself a [flex item](CSS-FLEXBOX#flex-item) in an outer flex container), it needs to submit the position of the baselines that will best represent its contents. To this end, the baselines of a flex container are determined as follows (after reordering with [order](CSS-DISPLAY-4#propdef-order), and taking [flex-direction](CSS-FLEXBOX#propdef-flex-direction) into account):

first/last ** main-axis baseline set** 

When the [inline axis](CSS-WRITING-MODES-4#inline-axis) of the [flex container](CSS-FLEXBOX#flex-container) matches its [main axis](CSS-FLEXBOX#main-axis), its baselines are determined as follows:

1.  If any of the [flex items](CSS-FLEXBOX#flex-item) on the flex container’s [startmost](CSS-WRITING-MODES-4#css-start) [flex line](CSS-FLEXBOX#flex-line) participate in first [baseline alignment](CSS-ALIGN-3#baseline-alignment) along the [main axis](CSS-FLEXBOX#main-axis), [generate](CSS-ALIGN-3#generate-baselines) a [baseline set](CSS-ALIGN-3#baseline-set) from their shared [alignment baseline](CSS-ALIGN-3#alignment-baseline) and the [flex container’s](CSS-FLEXBOX#flex-container) [first available font](CSS-FONTS-4#first-available-font).

2.  Otherwise, if any of the [flex items](CSS-FLEXBOX#flex-item) on the flex container’s [startmost](CSS-WRITING-MODES-4#css-start) [flex line](CSS-FLEXBOX#flex-line) participate in last [baseline alignment](CSS-ALIGN-3#baseline-alignment) along the [main axis](CSS-FLEXBOX#main-axis), [generate](CSS-ALIGN-3#generate-baselines) a [baseline set](CSS-ALIGN-3#baseline-set) from their shared [alignment baseline](CSS-ALIGN-3#alignment-baseline) and the [flex container’s](CSS-FLEXBOX#flex-container) [first available font](CSS-FONTS-4#first-available-font).

3.  Otherwise, if any [flex items](CSS-FLEXBOX#flex-item) in the [startmost](CSS-WRITING-MODES-4#css-start) [flex line](CSS-FLEXBOX#flex-line) have a [baseline set](CSS-ALIGN-3#baseline-set) along the [main axis](CSS-FLEXBOX#main-axis), take the baseline set from the first such flex item in [order-modified document order](CSS-DISPLAY-4#order-modified-document-order).

4.  Otherwise, if there are any [flex items](CSS-FLEXBOX#flex-item) at all, [synthesize](CSS-ALIGN-3#synthesize-baseline) a [baseline set](CSS-ALIGN-3#baseline-set) from the [startmost](CSS-WRITING-MODES-4#css-start) flex item on the startmost line.

5.  Otherwise, the [flex container](CSS-FLEXBOX#flex-container) has no first [main-axis](CSS-FLEXBOX#main-axis) [baseline set](CSS-ALIGN-3#baseline-set). (One is [synthesized](CSS-ALIGN-3#synthesize-baseline) from the flex container itself if needed, according to the rules of its [alignment context](CSS-ALIGN-3#shared-alignment-context).)

Last baselines are analogous (with “first”/“last” and “start”/“end” inverted).

first/last ** cross-axis baseline set** 

When the [inline axis](CSS-WRITING-MODES-4#inline-axis) of the [flex container](CSS-FLEXBOX#flex-container) matches its [cross axis](CSS-FLEXBOX#cross-axis), its baselines are determined as follows:

1.  If the flex container has at least one [flex item](CSS-FLEXBOX#flex-item), the flex container’s first/last [cross-axis baseline set](CSS-FLEXBOX#cross-axis-baseline) is [generated](CSS-ALIGN-3#generate-baselines) from the [alignment baseline](CSS-ALIGN-3#alignment-baseline) of the [startmost](CSS-WRITING-MODES-4#css-start)/[endmost](CSS-WRITING-MODES-4#css-end) flex item. (If that item has no alignment baseline parallel to the flex container’s [cross axis](CSS-FLEXBOX#cross-axis), then one is first [synthesized](CSS-ALIGN-3#synthesize-baseline) from its border edges.)

2.  Otherwise, the flex container has no first/last cross-axis [baseline set](CSS-ALIGN-3#baseline-set), and one is [synthesized](CSS-ALIGN-3#synthesize-baseline) if needed according to the rules of its [alignment context](CSS-ALIGN-3#shared-alignment-context).

When calculating the baseline according to the above rules, if the box contributing a baseline has an [overflow](CSS-OVERFLOW-3#propdef-overflow) value that allows scrolling, the box must be treated as being in its initial scroll position for the purpose of determining its baseline.

When [determining the baseline of a table cell](CSS2#height-layout), a flex container provides a baseline just as a line box or table-row does. \[CSS2\]

See [CSS Writing Modes 3 § 4.1 Introduction to Baselines](CSS-WRITING-MODES-3#intro-baselines) and [CSS Box Alignment 3 § 9 Baseline Alignment Details](CSS-ALIGN-3#baseline-rules) for more information on baselines.

